X:1
T:Chant reference take
C:one take, about 2 minutes; a bar of rest between patterns
M:2/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=72
K:clef=none
%
% 1  your example: the pickup crescendos into the downbeat   (bah, twice)
"^1 bah" z5/4 B//B//B// | B/B/ B//B//B/ | B/B/ B// z3/4 | z2 |
z5/4 B//B//B// | B/B/ B//B//B/ | B/B/ B// z3/4 | z2 |
% 2  your example: runs after rests, the last run leads to the last note
"^2" z5/4 B//B//B// | z//B//B//B// z//B//B//B// | z//B//B//B// B | z2 |
z5/4 B//B//B// | z//B//B//B// z//B//B//B// | z//B//B//B// B | z2 |
% 3  dotted eighth + sixteenth (the gap before the short note)
"^3" B/>B/ B | B/>B/ B/B/ | B2 | z2 |
B/>B/ B | B/>B/ B/B/ | B2 | z2 |
% 4  a held note into an anacrusis; a long last note
"^4" B3/2 B/ | B B/B/ | B2 | z2 |
B3/2 B/ | B B/B/ | B2 | z2 |
% 5  rests inside the pattern (do the dynamics start again after a rest?)
"^5" B/B/ z/B/ | B/B/ z | B/B/ B/B/ | B z | z2 |
B/B/ z/B/ | B/B/ z | B/B/ B/B/ | B z | z2 |
% 6  the same pattern as a statement, then as a question
"^6 statement" B B/B/ | B B | z2 |
"^6 question" B B/B/ | B B | z2 |
% 7  6/8
[M:6/8][Q:3/8=72] "^7" B/B/B/ B B/ | B3/2 B/B/B/ | B3 | z3 |
B/B/B/ B B/ | B3/2 B/B/B/ | B3 | z3 |
% 8  6/8 with a pickup
"^8" z5/2 B/ | B/B/B/ B B/ | B3/2 z3/2 | z3 |
z5/2 B/ | B/B/B/ B B/ | B3/2 z3/2 | z3 |
% 9  on syllables, once each: 1 (Du Ta De Ta ...), 3, 5, then 7 (Du Da Di)
[M:2/4][Q:1/4=72] "^9 syllables" z5/4 B//B//B// | B/B/ B//B//B/ | B/B/ B// z3/4 | z2 |
B/>B/ B | B/>B/ B/B/ | B2 | z2 |
B/B/ z/B/ | B/B/ z | B/B/ B/B/ | B z | z2 |
[M:6/8][Q:3/8=72] B/B/B/ B B/ | B3/2 B/B/B/ | B3 |]
